   "title": "Discussion: What Should America's Role in the World Be?",
   "html": "<p>Americans have argued about their country's role in the world since Washington's day. Some say the United States should lead and defend an open order of alliances and trade. Some say it has overreached and should look first to its own borders, economy, and people. Others seek a middle path. What do you think America's role should be?</p>\n<p><strong>Your post (about 100 to 150 words):</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Take a clear position: lead, hold back, or a middle path, and say in a sentence what you mean by it.</li>\n<li>Give one specific piece of evidence from the lesson \"September 11 and the War on Terror\" or the source George W. Bush, Address to a Joint Session of Congress that supports you.</li>\n<li>Name one fact that cuts against your position, and explain why you still hold it.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Your reply (about 50 to 75 words):</strong> Respond to one classmate. Do you agree with their reasoning? If so, strengthen it with something they did not use. If not, say respectfully where their reasoning falls short.</p>\n<p>Post first, then reply. You will not see your classmates' posts until you have posted.</p>",
